    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Add, inspect, and replace draft template packages in a draft.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nSUBCOMMANDS:\r\n  add                         Add a draft template package as a template segment.\r\n  publish                     Publish the current designer draft as a standard local template\r\n                              package.\r\n  render                      Compile template_config.json through Blueprint XML, apply it, and\r\n                              export MP4.\r\n  slots                       List replaceable slots inside an added template segment.\r\n  replace                     Replace one slot inside an added template segment.\r\n\r\nWORKFLOW\r\n  1. Find and download a template package through material.\r\n     material search   --type template --prompt \"travel vlog\"\r\n     material query    --type template --resource-id <template_id>\r\n     material download --type template --resource-id <template_id> --resource-dir /tmp/templates\r\n\r\n  2. Add the downloaded template package to a draft.\r\n     draft template add --ref local://demo --resource local:///tmp/templates/<template_id>.zip\r\n     draft template add --ref local://demo --resource template://<template_id>\r\n\r\n  3. Inspect replaceable slots, then replace them.\r\n     draft template slots   --ref local://demo --template-seg-id <template_segment_id>\r\n     draft template replace --ref local://demo --template-seg-id <template_segment_id> --slot <slot_id> --resource local:///abs/video.mp4\r\n\r\n",
